# [doc = " The Big5 encoding."] # [doc = ""] # [doc = " This is Big5 with HKSCS with mappings to more recent Unicode assignments"] # [doc = " instead of the Private Use Area code points that have been used historically."] # [doc = " It is believed to be able to decode existing Web content in a way that makes"] # [doc = " sense."] # [doc = ""] # [doc = " To avoid form submissions generating data that Web servers don't understand,"] # [doc = " the encoder doesn't use the HKSCS byte sequences that precede the unextended"] # [doc = " Big5 in the lexical order."] # [doc = ""] # [doc = " [Index visualization](https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/big5.html),"] # [doc = " [Visualization of BMP coverage](https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/big5-bmp.html)"] # [doc = ""] # [doc = " This encoding is designed to be suited for decoding the Windows code page 950"] # [doc = " and its HKSCS patched \"951\" variant such that the text makes sense, given"] # [doc = " assignments that Unicode has made after those encodings used Private Use"] # [doc = " Area characters."] # [doc = ""] # [doc = " This will change from `static` to `const` if Rust changes"] # [doc = " to make the referent of `pub const FOO: &'static Encoding`"] # [doc = " unique cross-crate, so don't take the address of this"] # [doc = " `static`."] pub static BIG5 : & 'static Encoding = & BIG5_INIT ;